<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Francisco de Campeche</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campeche">Campeche</a> is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-mexico">Gulf of Mexico</a>, capital of the Mexican state of Campeche. Founded by the Spanish in 1540 on the site of a Maya town, it became the main port of the Province of Yucatán and was repeatedly raided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a>, which led to the building of its walls and bastions in the late 17th and 18th centuries. Its fortified historic town is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-francisco-de-campeche.jpg" alt="San Francisco de Campeche" width="320" height="584" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: self. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montaje_de_San_Francisco_de_Campeche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
